# Changelog (released versions are frozen)

[CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) follows Keep a Changelog **groups**, but
**do not** use a `## [Unreleased]` section. Ever. New product notes go
under the current dated `## [x.y.z]`. When that version is already tagged,
add a new dated `## [x.y.z]` on the PR that completes the next version
(same PR as `__version__` / OpenAPI). Do not open a heading with no date.

Dated `## [x.y.z]` bullet text is **immutable** once tagged; do not rewrite
or “clarify” it. The current open version (not yet tagged) may still
receive new bullets.

`###` groups are **A–Z** in every version: Added, Changed, Deprecated,
Fixed, Removed, Security. Do not use Keep a Changelog’s
Removed-before-Fixed order. Omit unused groups.

**CHANGELOG = product. Website ≠ product.** Do not add, date, or “complete
a release” with website notes.

Website is `website/**` (Astro/Starlight source and the npm package in that
tree), `.github/workflows/pages.yml`, Pages artifacts (`website/dist/`,
cicerone.dev chrome), and anything that exists only to publish
cicerone.dev. `docs/*.md` is not website-only (see Borderline).

Product is the `cicerone` package: job, serve, dashboard app, events, I/O,
CLI, config, models.

If a train has both product and site changes, the current version gets
**only** the product bullets — no website bullet beside them. Site-only:
leave the current version unchanged. Empty new-version sections are not
required: `website/src/lib/changelog.mjs` `parseLatestRelease` uses the
first dated `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD`
(`website/src/lib/changelog.test.mjs`). No pytest/CI/tag/`publish.yml`
job requires a placeholder heading; do not invent any.

Split lives only in this file. Keep the `changelog.mdc` line in
[agent-policy-source.mdc](agent-policy-source.mdc) in sync; do not fork a
second copy of the split.

## Borderline

- `src/cicerone/static/cicerone-logo.svg` (dashboard): product.
  `website/src/assets/cicerone-logo.svg` only: not.
- Regenerating `docs/openapi/serve.openapi.json` because serve changed:
  product. Copy-only under `website/public/openapi/`: not.

## Do

- Put new notes under the current dated `## [x.y.z]` on the train you
  are targeting (patch on `main`, minor on `release/X.Y.0`), except when
  that version is already tagged — then start the next dated `## [x.y.z]`
  on the PR that completes it.
- Keep `###` headings A–Z. Reorder existing groups to match; do not
  rewrite tagged bullets.
- Short bullets for **this** product change. Do not re-tell older releases.

## Do not

- Changelog the website. Ever.
- Add `## [Unreleased]`. Ever.
- Rewrite, move, or “clarify” bullets in a tagged `## [x.y.z]` section.
- Re-document a shipped version inside a later heading
  (e.g. do not narrate 0.5.0 lock behavior inside a later HA note).
- Backport later items into an already-tagged release section.
